A||||3||loafer87gt||Does anyone know how to trace senders of email?||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||12-20-2000||01:50 AM||||Hey guys,I have been getting a bunch of messages lately from someone I don't know that contain infected zip files. Does anyone know how to track down the sender so I can file a complaint to their provider. Here is the info I have:<P><BR>Return-Path: &lt;loafer@sk.sympatico.ca&gt;<BR>Received: from raiden.sk.sympatico.ca ([142.165.5.180]) by<BR>          mss-03.fw.sk.sympatico.ca (Netscape Messaging Server 4.15 comet<BR>          Aug  8 2000 13:22:32) with ESMTP id G5UPLR00.FA1 for<BR>          &lt;loafer@mta-01.sk.sympatico.ca&gt;; Tue, 19 Dec 2000 23:22:39 -0600 <BR>Received: from localhost ([216.174.153.96])<BR>	by raiden.sk.sympatico.ca (8.9.3/8.9.3) with SMTP id XAA47548046<BR>	for &lt;loafer@sk.sympatico.ca&gt;; Tue, 19 Dec 2000 23:22:38 -0600 (CST)<BR>Message-Id: &lt;200012200522.XAA47548046@raiden.sk.sympatico.ca&gt;<BR>From: "Mailing Server" &lt;&gt;<BR>To: "Mailing list" &lt;&gt;<BR>Subject: Test mail<BR>Date: Tue, 19 Dec 2000 23:11:16 -0500<BR>MIME-Version: 1.0<BR>Content-Type: multipart/mixed;<BR>	boundary="--------"<BR>X-Mailer: Microsoft Outlook Express 4.0<P>---------------------------------------------<P>Anyway to get an IP address from this so Io can use Neotrace to find find who is sending me this junk? Thanks in advance<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-20-2000||02:05 AM||||From what I understand the person who sent it to you has mimic'd your Email The return path is your Email. So it would trace back to your local server. I think this is from those SPAM programs that allows mass-mailings and fills the return path with the address it is sending to. Not really a net expert so I can't say for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||12-20-2000||04:41 AM||||Yep.<P>Basically you traverse from top to bottom to follow the path in reverse back to the originator.<P>The reverse path is:<P>mss-02.fw.sk.sympatico.ca<BR>from<BR>raiden.sk.sympatico.ca<BR>from<BR>IP address 216.174.153.96 (which is the originator)<P>raiden.sk.sympatico.ca is running sendmail 8.9.3 which is pretty good at detecting and reporting spoofed IP addresses (and has functional anti-relay and anti-spam features) so this is probably the real address of the sending machine. It's pretty easy to spoof the reply-to address - I know a funny story about someone who did that as part of a joke that backfired on him. <P>There is no reverse-DNS entry for this host but looking at the whois database shows the netblock 216.174.153.0/24 as being assigned to ACCESSCOMM-NET8.<P>You should forward your complaint to "abuse@accesscomm.net". <BR><p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||12-20-2000||07:00 AM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.spamcop.net." TARGET=_blank>www.spamcop.net.</A>   Once you get signed up for the free service, you can cut and paste messages and it will figure out who to send the complaint to and do it for you.  That is, if it can figure out valid addresses, which it usually can...<P>Just remember to paste in the entire message, including the headers and all.||||reg||1
